they might crisscross across these towns and cities as everyone does. Everyone does in London, whether it's on the bus, the tube, et cetera. That's what was going on in Berlin. Even though it was East and West Berlin, there were zones of occupation, East Berliners under the Soviet zone could still travel to work in West Berlin. They could still go to the hospital or they could go and see relatives or friends. And that was the loophole. So if you're very clever and careful and you're not obviously showing
