2.1 million East Germans had fled to the West. Can I ask you then, so say the summer of 1961, I'm sure this is a really it's an impossible question, but I want to ask it anyway. Do you have a sense of how many what percentage of people in East Germany are true believers in communism? And what percentage are people who are desperate to get out? Well, I think you'd have to look at, if you talk about the latter, the latter is easy to look at because you look at statistics. Like I said, 2.1 million had left by 1961, and that's a sixth of the population. And from that sixth of the population, 50% of them were under 25 years old.
210万东德人逃往西方。那我能问你吗，比方说1961年夏天，我确信这是一个非常……这是一个不可能的问题，但无论如何我都想问。你有没有一种感觉，东德有多少人、百分之多少人是共产主义的真正信徒？又有多少百分比的人是急于离开的？好吧，我想你必须看看，如果你谈论后者，后者很容易看，因为你可以看统计数据。就像我说的，到1961年，有210万人离开，这占人口的六分之一。在这六分之一的人口中，50%的人在25岁以下。

