between the East German government and the Kremlin. So instead of a one-way traffic of orders, you will do this, you will do that, Ulbricht was allowed to obviously regularly visit the Kremlin, sit down with Khrushchev and tell him his problems. And they're all very aware. They're looking at the statistics. They're seeing this flood, this migratory flood
